From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Shape Healing - raise instead of dereferencing a null surface
 in ShapeAnalysis::GetFaceUVBounds

ShapeAnalysis::GetFaceUVBounds takes a shortcut when the face carries no edge:

  TopExp_Explorer ex(FF, TopAbs_EDGE);
  if (!ex.More())
  {
    TopLoc_Location L;
    BRep_Tool::Surface(F, L)->Bounds(UMin, UMax, VMin, VMax);
    return;
  }

BRep_Tool::Surface returns a null handle for a face with no surface, so a face
that is both surface-less and edgeless dereferences null. Both clauses are
needed: a surface-less face carrying a wire takes the pcurve loop below, where
the bounding box stays void and Bnd_Box2d::Get raises
Standard_ConstructionError, which is the behaviour the callers are written for.

ShapeUpgrade_ShapeDivide::Perform wraps ShapeUpgrade_FaceDivide::SplitSurface,
and so this call, in a try whose handler encodes ShapeExtend_FAIL2. The fault
lands exactly where that handler was meant to report, and only reaches it when
something unrelated has installed a signal handler, because OCC_CATCH_SIGNALS
converts a signal only while an OSD signal handler is registered. With none
registered the process dies. Measured on macOS arm64 against V8_0_1 with the
unpatched translation unit override-linked: exit 139 on
ShapeAnalysis::GetFaceUVBounds directly, on ShapeUpgrade_ShapeDivide::Perform
over a compound holding such a face, and on ShapeUpgrade_FaceDivide::Perform
called directly, which has no OCC_CATCH_SIGNALS above it at all.

Raising rather than returning, for three measured reasons.

The function's other failure path already raises. With edges but no pcurves the
box stays void and Bnd_Box2d::Get raises Standard_ConstructionError, so the
surface-less face with a wire is already reported as ShapeExtend_FAIL2. The two
input classes now agree instead of one crashing.

Returning without touching the outputs does not fix the crash, it moves it. No
caller checks a status, because the function is void, and every caller reads the
four doubles straight afterwards. ShapeUpgrade_FaceDivide::SplitSurface then
dereferences the same null surface eight lines later, at
surf->Bounds(aSUf, aSUl, aSVf, aSVl). Measured with a silent-return variant
override-linked: ShapeAnalysis::GetFaceUVBounds returns the caller's
uninitialised doubles unchanged, and ShapeUpgrade_ShapeDivide::Perform and
ShapeUpgrade_FaceDivide::Perform both still exit 139.

A raise is catchable unconditionally, a signal is not. An ordinary
catch (Standard_Failure const&) sees Standard_NullObject whether or not an OSD
signal handler was installed, which is what makes the existing FAIL2 handler
work rather than depending on unrelated process state.

With the patch, ShapeUpgrade_ShapeDivide::Perform over the compound answers
perform=false, Status(ShapeExtend_FAIL) and Status(ShapeExtend_FAIL2), which is
byte for byte what the surface-less-with-wire control already answered, and the
healthy box control and ShapeFix_Shape over the same compound are unchanged.

Four GTests in a new ShapeAnalysis_Test.cxx cover the raise, the
surface-less-with-wire neighbour, the no-edge branch's own valid input (a
spherical surface with no wires still reports the surface bounds) and a box face
for the pcurve branch. Against the unpatched source the first takes the process
down with signal 11; against the patched source all four pass.

SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#2773.
---
 .../TKShHealing/ShapeAnalysis/ShapeAnalysis.cxx        | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeAnalysis/ShapeAnalysis.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeAnalysis/ShapeAnalysis.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeAnalysis/ShapeAnalysis.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeAnalysis/ShapeAnalysis.cxx
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
 #include <ShapeAnalysis_Curve.hxx>
 #include <ShapeAnalysis_Edge.hxx>
 #include <ShapeExtend_WireData.hxx>
+#include <Standard_NullObject.hxx>
 #include <gp_Pnt.hxx>
 #include <NCollection_Sequence.hxx>
 #include <TopExp.hxx>
@@ -276,8 +277,14 @@ void ShapeAnalysis::GetFaceUVBounds(const TopoDS_Face& F,
   TopExp_Explorer ex(FF, TopAbs_EDGE);
   if (!ex.More())
   {
-    TopLoc_Location L;
-    BRep_Tool::Surface(F, L)->Bounds(UMin, UMax, VMin, VMax);
+    TopLoc_Location           L;
+    occ::handle<Geom_Surface> aSurf = BRep_Tool::Surface(F, L);
+    if (aSurf.IsNull())
+    {
+      // With no edges there is no pcurve to bound either, so nothing is left to report.
+      throw Standard_NullObject("ShapeAnalysis::GetFaceUVBounds: face has no surface");
+    }
+    aSurf->Bounds(UMin, UMax, VMin, VMax);
     return;
   }

